insert into public.budget_of_work (grade, subject, content_markdown, source_file)
values (
  3,
  'Computer',
  $bow$# Grade 3 Computer — Budget of Work

## Term 1: Parts, Care, and Basic Control of a Computer
- **Wk1-2: Identifying the computer and its parts.** Naming the main parts of a desktop or laptop (monitor, keyboard, mouse/trackpad, CPU/system unit, speakers) and describing the job of each in simple terms; distinguishing input devices (keyboard, mouse) from output devices (monitor, speakers, printer).
- **Wk3-4: Proper care, posture, and safety.** Practicing correct sitting posture, screen distance, and break habits to protect the eyes and body during computer use; handling hardware gently (no food/drinks near the keyboard, clean hands, no pulling cables); powering a computer on and off using the correct steps, including logging in and out safely.
- **Wk5-7: Mouse and keyboard control.** Practicing accurate single-click, double-click, right-click, and click-and-drag with the mouse to open, move, and resize windows and icons; identifying and correctly using letter keys, number keys, spacebar, enter, backspace, delete, shift, and arrow keys; opening and closing a simple application using an icon or menu.
- **Wk8-10: Building basic typing accuracy.** Practicing correct finger placement on the home row keys; typing one's own name, short words, and simple sentences with increasing accuracy; term project — following a short set of on-screen instructions from opening a program to closing it correctly.

## Term 2: Creating Simple Digital Work
- **Wk1-3: Introduction to a word-processing or drawing program.** Opening a word-processing or drawing application; typing and editing short text (own name, a sentence, a short list) — using backspace/delete to correct mistakes; using the toolbar to change font size, font color, and to bold or underline text.
- **Wk4-6: Drawing and simple formatting.** Using basic drawing tools (pencil/brush, shapes, fill color, eraser) to create a simple labeled picture (e.g., a picture of one's family or favorite animal with a caption); adding a short typed caption or title to a drawing.
- **Wk7-8: Saving and opening files, with adult guidance.** Saving a file with a sensible file name into a designated folder, with help; reopening a previously saved file to continue or review work; understanding why saving work regularly is important.
- **Wk9-10: Combining skills into a small project.** Creating one labeled drawing or one short typed paragraph (about a topic of choice, e.g., "My Family" or "My Favorite Animal") that combines typing, formatting, and saving skills learned this term; presenting the finished work to a partner or the class.

## Term 3: Introduction to the Internet and Staying Safe Online
- **Wk1-2: What is the internet?** Describing, in simple terms, what the internet is used for (finding information, watching videos, talking to family) and how a device connects to it; recognizing common icons for a web browser and a search engine.
- **Wk3-5: Staying safe online.** Identifying the difference between a safe, kid-friendly website (visited with an adult) and content that is not appropriate; understanding the rule of never sharing personal information (full name, address, school, password) online without a trusted adult's permission; recognizing that not everything seen online is true, and asking a trusted adult when unsure.
- **Wk6-7: Simple keyboard shortcuts and habits.** Learning a small set of useful shortcuts (e.g., using arrow keys to move a cursor, using backspace to fix typing) that speed up basic computer use; practicing closing a program and shutting down a computer correctly and safely.
- **Wk8-10: Term and year-end integration project.** Planning and creating a simple multimedia output that combines a labeled drawing and a short typed paragraph on a topic of the learner's choice (e.g., a favorite place or hobby), following safe-use habits practiced throughout the year, and presenting it to the class.$bow$,
  null
);
